window.docContents[229].resolve({"/Sub/#Type-Systems--Sub___-Subtyping--Concepts--The-Subtype-Relation--Summary":{"contents":"In summary, we form the STLC with subtyping by starting with the\npure STLC (over some set of base types) and then...\n\n* adding a base type ⊤,* adding the rule of subsumption\n\nΓ ⊢ t₁ ⦂ τ₁\n τ₁ <: τ₂\n-----------  (sub)\nΓ ⊢ t₁ ⦂ τ₂\n\n\nto the typing relation, and\n\n* defining a subtype relation as follows:\n\n                      σ <: υ\n                      υ <: τ\n                      ------                         (trans)\n                      σ <: τ\n\n                      ------                         (refl)\n                      τ <: τ\n\n                      ------                         (⊤)\n                      σ <: ⊤\n\n                     σ₁ <: τ₁\n                     σ₂ <: τ₂\n                ------------------                   (prod)\n                σ₁ × σ₂ <: τ₁ × τ₂\n\n                     τ₁ <: σ₁\n                     σ₂ <: τ₂\n                ------------------                   (arrow)\n                σ₁ → σ₂ <: τ₁ → τ₂\n\n                      n > m\n        ----------------------------------           (rcdWidth)\n        {i₁:τ₁...iₙ:τₙ} <: {i₁:τ₁...iₘ:τₘ}\n\n             σ₁ <: τ₁  ...  σₙ <: τₙ\n        ----------------------------------           (rcdDepth)\n        {i₁:σ₁...iₙ:σₙ} <: {i₁:τ₁...iₙ:τₙ}\n\n{i₁:σ₁...iₙ:σₙ} is a permutation of {j₁:τ₁...jₙ:τₙ}\n---------------------------------------------------  (rcdPerm)\n        {i₁:σ₁...iₙ:σₙ} <: {j₁:τ₁...jₙ:τₙ}\n\n\nSuppose we have  σ <: τ and υ <: δ.  Which of the following\nsubtyping assertions is false?(A) σ×υ <: ⊤(B) {i₁:σ,i₂:τ}→υ <: {i₁:σ,i₂:τ,i₃:δ}→υ(C) (σ→τ) → (⊤ → ⊤)  <:  (σ→τ) → ⊤(D) (⊤ → ⊤) → δ  <:  ⊤ → δ(E) σ → {i₁:υ,i₂:δ} <: σ → {i₂:δ,i₁:υ}\n\n(D). Applying the arrow rule requires ⊤ <: ⊤→⊤, but the only\nrule with ⊤ on the left is refl, and ⊤→⊤ ≠ ⊤, so there is no\nway to derive it.\n\nHow about these?(A) {i₁:⊤} <: ⊤(B) ⊤ → (⊤ → ⊤)  <:  ⊤ → ⊤(C) {i₁:τ} → {i₁:τ}  <:  {i₁:τ,i₂:σ} → ⊤(D) {i₁:τ,i₂:δ,i₃:δ} <: {i₁:σ,i₂:υ} × {i₃:δ}(E) ⊤ → {i₁:υ,i₂:δ} <: {i₁:σ} → {i₂:δ,i₁:δ}\n\n(D). The left-hand side is a record type and the right-hand side is\na product type; there is no rule relating the two type formers, so\nno record type can ever be a subtype of a product type, no matter\nhow its field types line up.\n\n","context":"Type Systems\u0009Sub: Subtyping\u0009Concepts\u0009The Subtype Relation","header":"8.1.4.6. Summary","id":"/Sub/#Type-Systems--Sub___-Subtyping--Concepts--The-Subtype-Relation--Summary"}});